1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,846
Deduction is where the exam separates candidates, so picture a scale of certainty.

2
00:00:05,846 --> 00:00:08,697
Must: the only possible explanation.

3
00:00:08,697 --> 00:00:11,145
The lights are off; they must have gone out.

4
00:00:11,145 --> 00:00:16,875
May, might or could: one of several possibilities: she may be in the library.

5
00:00:16,875 --> 00:00:19,270
And can't: impossible.

6
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:23,046
He can't be in Jumla; I saw him in Kathmandu an hour ago.

7
00:00:23,046 --> 00:00:27,994
Notice: the opposite of deductive must is can't, not mustn't.

